package tour;

// Base class for every demo in the tour. Each language-feature demo
// extends DemoClass and overrides execute() to walk that feature.
//
// Tour.run() builds an ArrayList<DemoClass>, pushes one instance of
// every subclass into it, then iterates the list calling execute()
// on each — so adding a new demo means writing a new .cajeta file
// here and one `demos.add(heap NewDemo());` line in Tour.cajeta.
//
// Cajeta has no formal `abstract` keyword today (see
// runtime/.../Stream.cajeta § "Abstract via empty-default convention"),
// so execute() lands as an empty concrete method; subclasses override
// via the `override` modifier. The base body is never invoked because
// every subclass overrides — but if someone forgets to override, the
// no-op silently passes rather than failing at compile time. Future
// work: real abstract-method support so forgetting an override is a
// compile-time error.
public class DemoClass {
    // Self-check counters, shared by every demo. check() below is the
    // tour's assertion: demos verify their own output instead of only
    // printing it, and Tour.main() turns any failure into a nonzero
    // exit code — so `cajeta run` doubles as the tour's test run.
    public static int32 checks = 0;
    public static int32 failures = 0;

    public void execute() {
    }

    // Assert `cond`; quiet when it holds, loud when it doesn't.
    public void check(boolean cond, String what) {
        DemoClass.checks = DemoClass.checks + 1;
        if (!cond) {
            DemoClass.failures = DemoClass.failures + 1;
            System.stdout.println("  FAIL: " + what);
        }
    }
}
